# Making Decisions about an Educational Game, Simulation or Workshop: A 'Game Theory' Perspective.

**Authors:** Cryer, Patricia

## Abstract
Uses game theory to help practitioners make decisions about educational games, simulations, or workshops whose outcomes depend to some extent on chance. Highlights include principles for making decisions involving risk; elementary laws of probability; utility theory; and principles for making decisions involving uncertainty. (eight references) (LRW)

